150
00:07:22,280 --> 00:07:30,440
And well, when we were talking about the suit, the person mentioned that all the suits are tailor-made.

151
00:07:31,100 --> 00:07:36,620
All right, this is a very important phrase if you want to go shopping for clothes that are made for you.

152
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:42,140
So something is tailor-made if the sizes are made only for fitting you.

153
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:42,680
That's right.

154
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:49,720
If you go to a department store and you buy a suit off of the shelf or the rack, it's not tailor-made.

155
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:55,040
But if the tailor makes it, he sews it to your size, then it's tailor-made.

156
00:07:55,040 --> 00:07:57,640
You know, wedding dresses are tailor-made.

157
00:07:57,640 --> 00:07:58,880
Special suits are tailor-made.

158
00:07:58,920 --> 00:08:01,620
So this is usually an expensive kind of clothing.

159
00:08:01,920 --> 00:08:06,210
Okay, so it basically means the tailor, the person, made it especially for you.

160
00:08:06,850 --> 00:08:09,450
And the opposite, as you said, would be off the rack.

161
00:08:09,790 --> 00:08:10,510
Off the rack.

162
00:08:10,670 --> 00:08:14,540
And this means that when you go to the store, you pick something, you like it, and you buy it.

163
00:08:15,520 --> 00:08:17,840
No one is going to sew it to make it fit you.

164
00:08:17,840 --> 00:08:18,020
That's right.

165
00:08:18,840 --> 00:08:21,200
And this is actually how most of us get our clothes.

166
00:08:21,200 --> 00:08:24,400
