167
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:25,800
Obviously all that stuff is off the rack.

168
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:27,760
It's not tailor-made for your size.

169
00:08:28,200 --> 00:08:28,340
That's right.

170
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:30,200
Okay.

171
00:08:30,200 --> 00:08:35,440
But if you really want to get something tailor-made, you need to be able to talk to the tailor about it.

172
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:37,880
So he will usually say, let me take your measurements.

173
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:39,360
This is our next phrase.

174
00:08:39,600 --> 00:08:39,960
That's right.

175
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:45,000
The tailor mentioned that he wants to take them over there and take his measurements.

176
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:52,480
So when the tailor says, I want to take your measurements or I need to take your measurements, what does that mean?

177
00:08:52,480 --> 00:08:57,020
That means I need to measure parts of your body to help make this suit.

178
00:08:57,640 --> 00:09:04,390
So he'll normally measure your shoulders, your waist, your hips, and how long things will be.

179
00:09:05,160 --> 00:09:05,750
So your arms and your legs.

180
00:09:06,160 --> 00:09:11,600
And these are all important measurements to know how big or how small to make the suit.

181
00:09:11,600 --> 00:09:12,600
That's right.

182
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:17,920
So you need to take your measurements or you can also say you have to get measured.

183
00:09:17,920 --> 00:09:18,070
That's right.

184
00:09:18,920 --> 00:09:22,280
So to get measured or to take someone's measurements.

185
00:09:22,280 --> 00:09:24,350
These are key phrases for buying a tailor-made suit.

